{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate", "label": "The Physical Review and the Release Gate", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_physical_review_md", "label": "PHYSICAL_REVIEW.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_physical_review", "label": "Physical Review", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Install it, launch it, use it on a machine carrying none of a development machine state; a green suite is a claim about the code talking to itself, not about the product."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_wp_review", "label": "WP-REVIEW", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ran a genuine fresh clone with isolated package cache and nothing on PATH but the pinned SDK; disproved undocumented machine state and non-deterministic first run, confirmed Linux would not launch."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_td_116_linux_launch_failure", "label": "TD-116 Linux Launch Failure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TypeLoadException during Avalonia X11 start-up from a security pin headless tests never exercise; left unfixed deliberately rather than choosing the trade-off implicitly, later resolved by WP 16.5B."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_td_45", "label": "TD-45", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Making CI Gate depend on the health check closed only the machine half; the branch-protection setting needed a repository administrator. A control with a machine half and a human half is not done when the machine half lands."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_td_42", "label": "TD-42", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "new-release.ps1 git tag and git push calls never check $LASTEXITCODE; confirm publication from the Release asset list, not a banner."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_wp_16_1a", "label": "WP 16.1A", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_wp_16_1a_r1_release_path_hardening", "label": "WP 16.1A-R1 Release Path Hardening", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "release.yml now runs the health check as a hard gate; new-release.ps1 requires the literal outcome success because a cancelled run is neither failure nor success; Linux smoke requires a positive log marker since a hung process looks identical to a healthy one at timeout."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_cancelled_is_not_success", "label": "Cancelled Is Not Success", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never treat did-not-fail as succeeded; a workflow run can conclude cancelled."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_diagnostic_step_cannot_fail_the_gate", "label": "Diagnostic Step Cannot Fail the Gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A summary step read a de-duplicated [1] filename as a wildcard and failed a run whose tests all passed; a step that only reports must be structurally unable to fail the gate it reports on."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_linux_launch_smoke", "label": "Linux Launch Smoke", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_mutation_testing_job", "label": "Mutation Testing Job", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_three_consecutive_green_ci_runs", "label": "Three Consecutive Green CI Runs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_release_gate_shape", "label": "Release Gate Shape", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Build both configurations with TreatWarningsAsErrors and grep every error or warning line rather than trust the exit code, dotnet test --no-build in both, health check 5/5, figures re-derived on the release-candidate commit and recorded in PROJECT_STATUS.md and Release Notes."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_ci_first_ran_at_release_time", "label": "CI First Ran at Release Time", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "v0.17.0 pushed nothing to a shared branch until the Product Owner Windows verification, so every gate figure to that point was local; a disclosed, deliberate weakening."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_defects_only_hands_find", "label": "Defects Only Hands Find", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WP 17.9.1-17.9.4 and WP 18.9.1 hotfixes came from the Product Owner walking the exact path a first-time user walks; no test had been asked to check them."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_bom_namespace_finding", "label": "BOM Namespace Finding", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deriving the same fact a second, different way found what re-reading the register harder never would."}, {"id": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_physical_review_nine_sections", "label": "PHYSICAL_REVIEW Nine Sections", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering Standards/08-the-physical-review-and-the-release-gate.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate", "target": "docs_academy_06_engineering_standards_08_the_physical_review_and_the_release_gate_physical_review_md", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/academy/06 Engineering